Wagtail is amazing! It did everything we needed and more. My primary frustration was in building reusable server-side rendered components and &quot;interactive islands&quot; (as popularized by Astro). The Django&#x2F;Jinja templating language can be pretty verbose and difficult to parameterize reusable functionality. I found myself constantly doing this:<p>```
      {% with field|contact_label as label %}
        &lt;div class=&quot;relative mt-5 my-3 md:my-5&quot;&gt;
          &lt;label class=&quot;{% if placeholders %}hidden{% endif %} bg-white absolute -top-[9px] block ml-2 px-2 text-black text-sm rounded&quot; for=&quot;{{ form_name }}_{{ field }}&quot;
            id=&quot;{{ form_name }}_{{ field }}_label&quot;&gt;
            {{ label }}
          &lt;&#x2F;label&gt;
```<p>(the &quot;with&quot; templatetag)<p>Over time these templates just became very difficult to work with. Part of that is likely also because I&#x27;ve been a full-time React dev for the better part of a decade, and I&#x27;m just faster with it.
